### Pause safely

**You own a clean stop. Leave a checkpoint a cold-start agent can resume from.** Explicit only. On "keep going", "going to bed, keep going", or "don't stop", don't pause.

1. Stop at a safe boundary. Finish the current atomic step or back out of it. Start nothing new. Cancel any nested subagents.
2. Take no irreversible action to pause. No PR and no push unless you already had one out.
3. Make the work durable. Commit uncommitted edits as one clear `wip:` commit on the current branch so nothing is lost. Tree broken? Say so in the commit body in one line.
4. Write the resume note off-context. Capture intent, what you were doing, progress and what's verified, current state, next steps, key files, gotchas. Compaction trigger: write it to a file like `/tmp/<slug>-resume.md`. A show-me-your-work trail exists? Point at it, don't duplicate.

**Reply:** where you are in the loop, what's on disk vs still in your head (paths, no diff dumps), the commits you made and whether the tree is clean, the first action on resume. A pause, not a final report.
